The glob view strips doc comment markers (`///`, `//!`) and drops a marker-only line ending the header, the same way file mode prints them; a marker-only line between two lines with text would end the header's first paragraph.
== args
input
== file input/doc.ts
/// Triple.
//! Bang.
//
export const x = 1;
== stdout
glob view: input
Includes only a header or summary per file.
For file-level outlines, use `outln [FILE]...`.
input/doc.ts: Triple. Bang.
== stderr
== exit 0
